---
/**
 * The component reference: one entry per family, generated from the same tables
 * the states gallery reads.
 *
 * ─── WHY THIS ROUTE IS THE LAST PAGE OF THE WAVE ──────────────────────────
 * Ten family cards printed ten matrices, and the states gallery folded them onto
 * one spine. What neither could answer is the question a contributor asks before
 * touching a component: what is this family FOR, what may I put in it, what is
 * it already asked to survive, and what may it never be? The matrices answer the
 * third cell by cell, and the fourth only by accident - a cell marked impossible
 * is a family saying what one of its parts may never be, and nobody had collected
 * those sentences in one place.
 *
 * This page is that collection. `Content/Specimen/Reference.ts` reads the ten
 * family modules - their `Rows`, their `Columns`, their `MatrixCell`, their
 * `Specimens`, their `Improvements` - and states each family in the same five
 * questions. It writes no sixth opinion: every figure, every column, every
 * prohibition and every proof row is read from the family itself.
 *
 * ─── THIS PAGE IS A LAB SURFACE ───────────────────────────────────────────
 * Like `/Specimen` and `/Specimen/States` it is a tool for the owner and the
 * agents, not a chapter for a reader: served in development, absent from the
 * production build. `Function/Configuration/Lab.mjs` lists it in `LabRoute`,
 * `Function/Route/Lab.ts` removes the emitted directory before the route map is
 * generated, and the sitemap filter keeps it out of `sitemap-0.xml`.
 *
 * ─── THE COMPOSITION: CONTRACT, FAMILIES, REGISTER ────────────────────────
 * The page is read in the order the document's constitution is read:
 *
 *   head           # SPECIMEN_03, the h1 at L, the `↳` proposition, STATUS: VERIFIED
 *   /THE CONTRACT  the seven laws that hold before any family's matrix is read,
 *                  each with what it means and how a reviewer checks it
 *   /THE FAMILIES  ten entries, each a disclosure: shut, the purpose, the figures
 *                  and the proof row; open, the slots, the columns, the
 *                  prohibitions, the matrix, the proof and what changed
 *   /THE REGISTER  what the reference counted, and the ten files it counted from
 *
 * ─── THE ONE XL IS NOT SPENT HERE ─────────────────────────────────────────
 * The head's `h1` is L, by the shell family's contract. The reference's largest
 * type is a prohibition's own sentence, which is what the page is about - and a
 * page that spent the XL on its own title would be claiming the rank of the
 * material band on `/Specimen`, which is not this page's subject.
 *
 * ─── NO NUMBER IS WRITTEN HERE ────────────────────────────────────────────
 * Every count is derived: the families, the slots, the cells, the prohibitions
 * and the resolved proofs from `Content/Specimen/Reference.ts`, which reads them
 * from the ten family modules. A figure typed into this file would be the one
 * number on the page that could disagree with the page.
 */
import { Header } from "../../Component/Layout/Header";
import Onward from "../../Component/More/Onward.astro";
import RecordBand from "../../Component/Record/RecordBand.astro";
import RecordLedger from "../../Component/Record/RecordLedger.astro";
import { RegisterOf } from "../../Component/Record/RegisterLine.js";
import Trail from "../../Component/Route/Trail.astro";
import SpecimenReference from "../../Component/Specimen/SpecimenReference.astro";
import SurfaceShell from "../../Component/Surface/SurfaceShell.astro";
import { Row } from "../../Component/Surface/State.js";
import {
	Bands,
	EntryCount,
	Head,
	LawCount,
	MatrixCells,
	Onward as OnwardCopy,
	ProofCount,
	Register,
	SlotCount,
} from "../../Content/Specimen/Reference.js";
import Base from "../../Layout/Base.astro";

const MetaTitle = "Reference | Code Editor Land";

const MetaDescription = `The component reference: ${EntryCount} families, one entry each - what the family is for, the ${SlotCount} parts a page may mount, the states and combinations it is asked, the ${LawCount} prohibitions its own matrix states in its own words, and the one live row that proves it, across ${MatrixCells} cells of the ten family matrices.`;

/** The trail: the index, the sheet, the gallery, then this reference. A crumb is a place. */
const TrailItems = [
	{ label: "/HOME", href: "/" },
	{ label: "/SPECIMEN", href: "/Specimen" },
	{ label: "/STATES", href: "/Specimen/States" },
	{ label: "/REFERENCE" },
];

/** The register's rows, and the line that counts them.
 *
 * `Register` is the rows themselves: `Content/Specimen/Reference.ts` counts
 * every figure at module load, so there is nothing for a call to decide, and
 * `Register()` throws `TypeError: Register is not a function` at prerender.
 * `RegisterOf` is what turns the rows into the counted line.
 */
const RegisterRows = Register;

const CountedRegister = RegisterOf("REGISTER", RegisterRows);
---

<Base
	Title={MetaTitle}
	Description={MetaDescription}
	Url={Astro.url.href}
	lang="en"
>
	<Header client:load slot="Header" />

	{/* The crumb sits above the shell, the way every surface's does: the trail
	    is a route statement about the page, and the head is the page's own
	    opening. A crumb printed under a title reads as a footnote to it. */}
	<Trail trail={TrailItems} class="reference-page__trail" />

	<SurfaceShell
		index={Head.index}
		title={Head.title}
		standfirst={Head.proposition}
		states={[Row("REFERENCE", "VERIFIED")]}
		rows={[
			{ key: "FAMILIES:", value: String(EntryCount) },
			{ key: "SLOTS:", value: String(SlotCount) },
			{ key: "PROHIBITIONS:", value: String(LawCount) },
			{ key: "PROOFS:", value: `${ProofCount} OF ${EntryCount}` },
		]}
	>
		{/* ─── THE CONTRACT ────────────────────────────────────────── */}
		<RecordBand band={{ ...Bands.Contract, id: "contract" }}>
			<SpecimenReference part="contract" />

			<p class="reference-page__note">
				These seven hold before any family's own matrix is read, and they
				are the only sentences on this page that are not derived: they are
				the document's constitution, restated as a table because a
				contributor reads a table and skips a paragraph. Each names the
				section it comes from and the thing a reviewer looks at - a law
				with no check is a preference.
				{` `}A family's own laws come after its slots, and they are the
				other way round: those are the sentences the family's matrix
				already uses to forbid a combination, collected rather than
				written.
			</p>
		</RecordBand>

		{/* ─── THE FAMILIES ────────────────────────────────────────── */}
		<RecordBand band={{ ...Bands.Families, id: "families" }}>
			<SpecimenReference part="families" />

			<p class="reference-page__note">
				Ten entries in `/Specimen`'s order, so a reader who uses the two
				pages together finds the same family in the same place. Each entry
				answers five questions in the same sequence - what the family is
				for, its slots, what it is asked, what it may never be, and the row
				that proves it - so comparing two families is comparing the same
				questions rather than two authors' habits.
				{` `}The matrix inside an entry is the family's OWN, not the
				gallery's spine: a cell that cannot exist prints `N/A` and a
				number, and the number is a link to the sentence that explains it.
				A sentence in a six-rem cell would be an excuse; a bare `N/A` with
				nothing to resolve it would be a hole. The number is the only
				arrangement that is both readable and complete.
				{` `}The proof row is a claim with a destination: it prints the
				row's own mark, its state and the sentence that says when the state
				is right, then links to the live row on the states gallery and to
				the family's own matrix. A proof a reader cannot go and look at is
				not a proof.
			</p>
		</RecordBand>

		{/* ─── THE REGISTER ────────────────────────────────────────── */}
		<RecordBand band={{ ...Bands.Register, id: "register" }}>
			<RecordLedger rows={RegisterRows} register={CountedRegister} />

			<p class="reference-page__note">
				Every figure above is counted from the ten family modules, and the
				source row names the files it was counted from. The two
				denominators are printed apart on purpose: an entry's own matrix is
				its rows against its own columns, and the spine is the same rows
				against the gallery's twenty-two conditions - a page that added the
				two would be counting one component twice.
				{` `}The proof row is the only thing on this page that was chosen
				rather than derived, and even it cannot drift: the mark is named in
				`Reference.ts` and resolved against the family's `Specimens`, so a
				row that moves out of a family leaves `◎ PROOF: UNAVAILABLE` behind
				instead of a pointer to a row nobody prints.
			</p>

			<Onward slot="foot" rows={OnwardCopy.rows} copy={OnwardCopy.copy} />
		</RecordBand>
	</SurfaceShell>
</Base>
